A capability is a named action with a typed contract and a handler.
Code mode combines calls to those actions in one program.
MCP (Model Context Protocol) lets an agent discover and call tools.

ratstack.sh already offers code mode:

- `POST /api/execute`.
- The MCP `execute` tool.

One request runs an async function body that combines content calls. [Joel's reply](https://x.com/joelhooks/status/2106018556496457773) asks for this alongside CLI, API, and MCP.

## A live program

This program runs against the live HTTP endpoint.

The callable definitions are in [`apps/mischief/src/capabilities/index.ts` at `445b1a20b51a5492f8e586daeb9306e8011b7673`, lines 34–45](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/445b1a20b51a5492f8e586daeb9306e8011b7673/apps/mischief/src/capabilities/index.ts#L34-L45). We wrote this read-only request.

```js
const found = await tools.search({ query: "cartridges", limit: 1 });
const page = await tools.read({ id: found.matches[0].id });
const graph = await tools.backlinks({ slug: page.routePath.split("/").at(-1) });
return { title: page.title, id: page.id, links: graph.backlinks.length };
```

The program passes the search result directly to read and reduces the graph result before returning it.

`POST /api/execute` returned this response on 2026-10-02:

```json
{"logs":[],"result":{"title":"Cartridges","id":"ratstack://lore/cartridges","links":31}}
```

Three typed calls use one outer request. This run measures neither latency nor token savings.

## The sandbox preserves the boundary

[`apps/mischief/src/capabilities/index.ts`](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/main/apps/mischief/src/capabilities/index.ts) builds `toExecuteCapability(contentCapabilities)`. That list contains search, read, backlinks, neighbors, mentions, and path.

`joinInterest` belongs to the outer API/MCP registry. It does not belong to the sandbox's callable list.

[`packages/capability/src/to-code-mode.ts`](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/main/packages/capability/src/to-code-mode.ts) builds the catalog and TypeScript declarations. Every call from sandbox code returns to application code that validates input and runs the handler.
That code encodes the output or declared failure.

[`sandbox-worker-loader.ts`](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/main/apps/mischief/src/sandbox-worker-loader.ts) runs a fresh Dynamic Worker, a Worker loaded to execute sandbox code, with:

- No outbound network.
- A 100 ms CPU limit.
- Five subrequests.
- A ten-second timeout.

Imports, exports, and fetch are unavailable.

The [HTTP and MCP rate-limit checks](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/main/apps/mischief/src/app.ts) use [native rate limits](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/main/apps/mischief/src/rate-limits.ts):

- Six execute calls per IP per minute.
- 300 execute calls total per minute.
- Separate counters in each Cloudflare location.

Combining calls does not waive these limits.

Use the [agent guide](/llms.txt) for the endpoint and call format. See [MCP](/lore/mcp-is-another-surface) for the tool transport.

See [how we do it with Effect](/lore/how-we-do-it-with-effect) for the whole path.
